     "idea": "**Settled**\n\n- Bonded Cl, Br, I carry anisotropic charge with a positive σ-hole; strength I > Br > Cl, tuned by electron-withdrawing groups and hybridisation {{politzer-trend}} {{cavallo-hybrid}}.\n- Contacts are strongly directional and short {{desiraju-angle}} {{michalczyk-csd}}.\n- CCSD(T)/CBS interaction energies are the reference, and benchmark sets exist {{rezac-x40}} {{kriz-sh250}}.\n- Delocalisation error makes low-exact-exchange functionals over-bind {{otero-delocal}}.\n\n**Debated**\n\n- How much is charge transfer, and is it separable from polarisation? {{wang-ct}} {{rezac-ct}} {{clark-notseparable}}\n- Which term causes linearity: electrostatics, exchange–repulsion, or CT plus Pauli? {{stone-jacs-linear}} {{huber-linear}}\n- Do dispersion corrections help or hurt for halogen bonds? It depends on the functional {{kozuch-disp}} {{otero-delocal}}.\n- Which isodensity surface and descriptor define 'the' σ-hole size? {{sedlak-flattening}} {{thirman-trend}}\n\n**Open**\n\n- A transferable acidity/basicity scale that covers neutral and anionic acceptors: existing single-parameter scales need one line per acceptor {{engelage-eq}} {{engelage-cationic}}.\n- Force fields for halogen bonds to **anions**: are virtual sites plus fixed charges enough, or are polarisation and charge penetration required? {{rackers-cp}} {{wang-cp}}\n- Polar flattening in force fields: anisotropic repulsion instead of spheres?\n- Fit targets: how to combine monomer data, QM scans and liquid data without double counting.",
